      "from": "SubagentStop",
      "to": "logstop",
      "label": "appends one log line"
    }
  ],
  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Four Hooks, Four Moments",
      "items": [
        "PreToolUse gates every Bash call, before it ever reaches the shell",
        "WorktreeRemove frees the pane and processes a worktree was holding",
        "SessionStart(compact) re-arms role contracts lost to compaction; SubagentStop just logs the exit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The Guard Runs Before, Never After",
      "items": [
        "hook-git-guard.py decides allow or block before the command executes",
        "A block writes to stderr and appends a line — the command never runs",
        "There is no retry loop: a block ends the attempt, it does not queue a review"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "State Lives in a Flat Log",
      "items": [
        "Every WorktreeRemove, SubagentStop, and missing-script event lands in one file",
        "/tmp/harness-hook-events.log is diagnostic only — it is not the tracker",
        "A missing hook script still logs and warns instead of failing silently"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
